      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Frame the safety net not as a cushion, but as a gilded cage that erodes personal responsibility. By guaranteeing a baseline of support, democratic socialism removes the essential incentive for individuals to strive, innovate, or take entrepreneurial risks. This creates a permanent class of dependents reliant on government handouts rather than empowered citizens. Ultimately, their \"help\" becomes a mechanism for societal stagnation, trapping people in a cycle of dependency.",
      "source": "target",
