      "content": "The argument for wealth redistribution as \"correcting history\" is a convenient moral smokescreen for punitive taxation. You can argue that while past injustices are real, constantly punishing current success to retroactively fix history punishes the present. Furthermore, it ignores the fundamental principle that individuals earn their wealth through risk and labor, and seizing it is a form of theft, regardless of the historical context. This framing shifts the focus from genuine opportunity to perpetual grievance.",
      "source": "target",
